sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Browser as Browser
  participant API as AuthController and AuthService
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant MailWorker as Verification email worker
  participant SES as AWS SES v2

  Browser->>API: POST /auth/signup with email only
  API->>API: Canonicalize email, rate limit, derive versioned verification token
  API->>DB: BEGIN pending registration and durable email outbox intent
  Note over API,DB: Store only token digests and frozen delivery metadata
  DB-->>API: COMMIT
  API-->>Browser: 202 accepted

  MailWorker->>DB: Claim available email row with lease
  DB-->>MailWorker: Pending registration identity and frozen payload inputs
  MailWorker->>MailWorker: Reconstruct token from UUID, key version, and server pepper
  MailWorker->>SES: SendEmail with a stable non-secret delivery tag
  Note over MailWorker,SES: Provider acceptance can precede a lost response or timeout
  alt Provider acceptance observed
    SES-->>MailWorker: Provider message ID
    MailWorker->>DB: Mark sent only while the lease token still owns the row
    Note over MailWorker,DB: If the process dies or acknowledgement times out here,<br/>the lease expires and a retry may send the email again
    Note over Browser,SES: A duplicate carries the same expiring single-use token.<br/>The delivery tag is correlation metadata, not provider idempotency
  else Retryable or ambiguous provider failure
    SES-->>MailWorker: Throttle, transient error, or timeout after unknown acceptance
    MailWorker->>DB: Clear lease and schedule bounded retry
  else Terminal or exhausted failure
    MailWorker->>DB: Record terminal failure without exposing secrets
  end

  Browser->>API: POST /auth/email-verifications/consume with link token
  API->>DB: Lock pending registration, compare digest, install enrollment digest
  DB-->>API: Verification consumed once
  API-->>Browser: 204 and HttpOnly enrollment cookie

  Browser->>API: GET /auth/registrations/current with enrollment cookie
  API->>DB: Validate unexpired enrollment digest
  API-->>Browser: ready

  Browser->>API: POST /auth/registrations/complete with name and password
  API->>API: Validate then hash password outside the row lock
  API->>DB: Lock enrollment, insert user and session digest, mark completed
  DB-->>API: COMMIT public user
  API-->>Browser: Clear enrollment cookie and set HttpOnly session cookie

  Browser->>API: Protected request with session cookie
  API->>DB: Digest lookup, revoke and expiry checks, bounded touch
  DB-->>API: Frozen principal and public user
  API-->>Browser: Authenticated response
